resources.string:
WFAS v2 is the previous version of the protocol. It stays available for devices that cannot be updated yet, but it is outdated and has known weaknesses that v3 fixes:

- protection is optional: without a key anyone on the network can connect, and the audio travels unencrypted;
- with a shared key, a weak passphrase can be guessed by whoever records the traffic, and whoever obtains the key can also decrypt sessions recorded in the past;
- the server announces itself to the whole network, and those announcements can be faked;
- in multicast, any receiver can insert audio in the name of the server.

Staying on v3 is recommended. If you turn v2 on, v3 is turned off until you switch back.
